// Cone calorimeter-like 1D PMMA simulation (ThermaKin2Ds .cnd)
// Generated to match the Julia example (06_cone_calorimeter.jl):
// - Thickness: 5.8 mm
// - External radiant heat flux: 0.9813*25 kW/m2 = 24.5325 kW/m2 (constant)
// - Top boundary: convection + re-radiation losses, gas allowed to escape
// - Bottom boundary: adiabatic and impermeable
// - 15% moisture content on the dry basis

OBJECT TYPE: 1D

OBJECT STRUCTURE
****************
THICKNESS:  0.012
TEMPERATURE:   300
MASS FRACTIONS:
DF  0.870
MOISTURE_1  0.130

THICKNESS:	1e-5
TEMPERATURE:	300
MASS FRACTIONS:
INERT	1.0

OBJECT BOUNDARIES
*****************

TOP BOUNDARY

MASS TRANSPORT: YES
DF_gas1  LIN  0.05  0
DF_gas2  LIN  0.05  0
DF_gas3  LIN  0.05  0
DF_gas4  LIN  0.05  0
DF_gas5	 LIN  0.05  0
WATER_VAPOR LIN  0.05  0

OUTSIDE INIT TEMP:   330
OUTSIDE HEAT RATE:   0   0   0   0
CONVECTION COEFF:    7.2

EXTERNAL RADIATION:  YES
TIME PROG1:          50.672e3  0   1e4
TIME PROG2:          0          0   0
REPEAT:              NO
ABSORPTION MODE:     RAND

FLAME:               NO

BOTTOM BOUNDARY

MASS TRANSPORT: NO

OUTSIDE INIT TEMP:   300
OUTSIDE HEAT RATE:   0   0   0   0
CONVECTION COEFF:    0

EXTERNAL RADIATION:  NO

FLAME:               NO

INTEGRATION PARAMETERS
**********************

ELEMENT SIZE:      1e-5
TIME STEP:         1e-3
DURATION:          1000

OUTPUT FREQUENCY:
ELEMENTS:          1
TIME STEPS:        1000
